        <type>std::pair&lt; nlohmann::json, std::vector&lt; std::string &gt; &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::pair&lt; nlohmann::json, std::vector&lt; std::string &gt; &gt; themis::utils::PIIPseudonymizer::pseudonymize</definition>
        <argsstring>(const nlohmann::json &amp;data)</argsstring>
        <name>pseudonymize</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::utils::PIIPseudonymizer::pseudonymize</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const nlohmann::json &amp;</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Pseudonymize detected PII in JSON object. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Replaces PII values with UUIDs. Requires a valid pseudonymization key; if the key is unavailable, the operation fails closed rather than producing plaintext in the output.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input JSON with potential PII </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>JSON with PII replaced by UUIDs, and list of UUID mappings created </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if pseudonymization key is unavailable (fail-closed)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
@error_contract <table rows="3" cols="5"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Condition  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1utils_1a06bcf365c98dd5d12c5d9b66705c6ac7" kindref="member">ErrorCode</ref>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Severity  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Logging  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Recovery  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Pseudonymization key unavailable (RAND_bytes failure)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>CRYPTO_KEY_DERIVATION_FAILED (9050)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Critical  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>key_id  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Throw (fail-closed – no plaintext produced)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Database unavailable (cannot persist mapping)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>CRYPTO_KEY_NOT_FOUND (9053)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Critical  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>pii_uuid  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Throw (fail-closed)  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>@degradation fail-closed – key unavailable → reject; never returns unredacted data on error <simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1utils_1a06bcf365c98dd5d12c5d9b66705c6ac7" kindref="member">ErrorCode</ref> 9050-9059 for crypto error taxonomy </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1utils_1a06bcf365c98dd5d12c5d9b66705c6ac7" kindref="member">ErrorCode</ref> 9040-9049 for privacy detection taxonomy </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
