    <briefdescription>
<para>PII Pseudonymization Manager with DSGVO Art. 17 compliance. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>DSGVO Art. 17 Compliant PII Management:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Replace detected PII with UUIDs in entities</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Store encrypted PII→UUID mapping in separate RocksDB Column Family</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_p_i_i_pseudonymizer_1acbc227fd9ea175d2a205a7915d09f59a" kindref="member">revealPII()</ref>: Decrypt and return original value (with audit log)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_p_i_i_pseudonymizer_1a880e25155c10a7748149c3c44e85ebf1" kindref="member">erasePII()</ref>: Delete mapping → original value irrecoverable</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Workflow:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Entity import: Detect PII → Replace with UUID → Store mapping</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Query: Entity contains UUIDs, original values hidden</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Reveal: Authorized user → decrypt PII mapping → log access</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Erasure: Delete mapping → UUID remains, but original lost forever </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
